    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want a DRAGON network between DNA methylation and gene expression for 45 patients. Both tables are continuous and have the same sample ID format. I'm not sure whether the methylation and the expression came from the same patients or from two separate cohorts that just happen to be the same size."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Do the methylation and expression data come from the same patients?\n  You wrote: \"I'm not sure whether the methylation and the expression came from the same patients or from two separate cohorts that just happen to be the same size\". DRAGON's contract: \"Layer 2 is reordered to layer 1 only after exact sample-ID set equality is proven\".\n- Were the different omics tables measured on the same samples?\n  You wrote: \"I'm not sure whether the methylation and the expression came from the same patients or from two separate cohorts that just happen to be the same size\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: I want a DRAGON network between DNA methylation and gene expression for 45 patients. Both tables are continuous and have the same sample ID format. I'm not sure whether the methylation and the expression came from the same patients or from two separate cohorts that just happen to be the same size.\nUser follow-up: They are two separate cohorts."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want a DRAGON network between DNA methylation and gene expression for 45 patients.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. DRAGON gives: one undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
